<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51262" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vōcĭfĭco</span></b> ,
			āre, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a.</i> [vox-facio],
				<i>to cry aloud</i>, <i>utter a loud
				cry</i>, <i>proclaim</i> (ante- and post-class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(apes) a se eiciunt fucos, quos vocificantes
					persequuntur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 16, 8</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>:  cujus vim Demosthenis
			orationes vocificant, <i><span class="en">Gell. 9, 3, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
